    "result_text": "I agree with the finding and addressed it. The three-signal risk rule was genuinely duplicated \u2014 a named, Javadoc'd business rule in V1 and an anonymous copy of the same OR-expression in V2, which would drift silently.\n\n**Fix:** I gave the aggregation a single home in the service layer, `ClinicService.isOwnerRiskFlagged(possibleDuplicate, email, city)`, which composes the two existing predicates (`isEmailDomainDisposableAdjacent`, `isCityOverSoftCapacity`) plus the duplicate flag. Both controllers now just call it and `setRiskFlag(...)`:\n\n- Removed the private `computeRiskFlag` helper from `OwnerRestControllerV1`.\n- Replaced the inlined expression in `OwnerRestControllerV2` with the same service call.\n\nThe spec's OR-composition now lives in exactly one place; adding a fourth signal touches only the service. I kept `possibleDuplicate` as a passed-in boolean (rather than re-deriving it in the service) because it originates from the persisted `Owner`/DTO, not from a store query like the other two \u2014 the controller unwraps the nullable DTO getter and hands the service a plain boolean.\n\nTests remain green: `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
